  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieved 0.485 accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) was much weaker at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. With only 2 data points, the key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can substantially improve over the linear PCA baseline. This experiment isolates the encoder variable (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000) while keeping profile_setting=singleprofile and model_setting=rna_only fixed, making it a clean single-factor comparison. If scvi_n200 outperforms PCA, it informs the choice of RNA encoder for all subsequent multimodal and multiprofile experiments; if it does not, PCA remains the default and we can pivot to testing multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion. This is the highest-information experiment available because the RNA encoder choice is a foundational design decision that affects every downstream configuration."
}

